\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Mini Jarvis - Phase 17R-D3 Storage Stability Addendum
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Project: Mini Jarvis\
Owner: Tony Provenzano\
Platform: Raspberry Pi 5 Model B Rev 1.1, 16GB RAM\
Operating System: Debian GNU/Linux 13, trixie\
Addendum Date: May 1, 2026\
Phase Status: COMPLETE / PASSED\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 1. Purpose of This Addendum
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This addendum documents the storage stability issue discovered after Phase 17R and the corrective action applied in Phase 17R-D3. It should be appended to the Mini Jarvis canonical documentation and included in the future public GitHub documentation package for all readers.\
The issue was not caused by the Mini Jarvis GUI, Ollama, conversation logging permissions, or the language model. The evidence pointed to USB SSD instability involving the JMicron USB-to-SATA bridge used by the boot drive.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 2. Phase Title
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Phase 17R-D3 - USB SSD UAS Stability Patch\
Purpose: Disable UAS for the JMicron SSD bridge so the Raspberry Pi 5 uses the more stable usb-storage driver path for the boot SSD.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 3. Problem Observed
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 After Mini Jarvis was left running overnight in Fast mode, the system produced a non-fatal conversation logging warning:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 [Warning: conversation log was not saved: [Errno 5] Input/output error: '/home/minijarvis/minijarvis/logs/conversations']\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Because of the earlier Phase 17R non-fatal logging patch, Mini Jarvis still returned an answer instead of failing the user interaction. However, additional symptoms showed that the problem was broader than the logging function.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\fi-180\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	Mini Jarvis GUI remained partially visible and could still accept some typed input.\
\'95	Mouse movement worked, but some desktop menus and dropdowns became non-responsive.\
\'95	The desktop background and menu bar degraded or disappeared during interaction.\
\'95	SSH connections from the Mac mini timed out or failed while the Pi was in the degraded state.\
\'95	The system later displayed a boot halt screen during recovery, then booted correctly after a reboot.\
\'95	The boot halt suggested storage or boot-file access instability rather than an application-only failure.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 4. Initial Concern: Was Logging Broken?
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The first question was whether conversation logging had ever worked and whether the log folder had a permissions problem. This was ruled out.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\fi-180\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	The conversation log folder existed at /home/minijarvis/minijarvis/logs/conversations/.\
\'95	Existing conversation logs were found for April 29, April 30, and May 1.\
\'95	A May 1 conversation log successfully contained a Fast-mode test question and Mini Jarvis answer.\
\'95	A direct log write test passed after reboot.\
\'95	Directory ownership and permissions were correct for the minijarvis user.\
\'95	The root filesystem was mounted read/write after reboot.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Conclusion: conversation logging works. The Errno 5 warning was a symptom of temporary storage I/O failure, not a logging-code or permissions failure.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 5. Evidence Collected
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The post-reboot diagnostic identified the USB SSD bridge as a JMicron device:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Bus 003 Device 003: ID 152d:0562 JMicron Technology Corp. / JMicron USA Technology Corp. JMS567 SATA 6Gb/s bridge\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The kernel log showed repeated UAS command aborts and a USB storage reset:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 sd 0:0:0:0: [sda] tag#24 uas_eh_abort_handler ...\
scsi host0: uas_eh_device_reset_handler start\
usb 3-2: reset high-speed USB device number 3 using xhci-hcd\
scsi host0: uas_eh_device_reset_handler success\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 These messages indicate instability in the USB Attached SCSI path for the SSD bridge. This class of issue can manifest as intermittent I/O errors, system stalls, desktop degradation, SSH loss, and boot instability.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 6. What Was Ruled Out
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\fi-180\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	Not a Mini Jarvis GUI logic failure.\
\'95	Not an Ollama model failure.\
\'95	Not a Qwen2.5 or Qwen3 model-selection issue.\
\'95	Not a conversation logging permission problem.\
\'95	Not a missing log directory problem.\
\'95	Not a full disk problem. Disk usage remained around 9 percent.\
\'95	Not a root filesystem read-only state after reboot. The root filesystem remounted read/write.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 7. Diagnosis
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Root cause class: USB SSD / JMicron UAS instability.\
The boot SSD is attached through a JMicron JMS567 SATA bridge with USB vendor/product ID 152d:0562. The Linux kernel initially used UAS for this device. The observed uas_eh_abort_handler and device reset messages indicate that the UAS path was unstable for this hardware combination on the Raspberry Pi 5.\
Corrective strategy: force this specific USB storage bridge to ignore UAS and use the older, more conservative usb-storage driver instead. This may reduce peak disk performance slightly, but it is usually preferable for appliance reliability. Mini Jarvis does not require maximum SSD throughput during normal operation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 8. Patch Applied
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 File changed:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Kernel command-line parameter added:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 usb-storage.quirks=152d:0562:u\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Final cmdline.txt content after patch:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 console=serial0,115200 console=tty1 root=PARTUUID=3ad44b93-02 rootfstype=ext4 fsck.repair=yes rootwait quiet splash plymouth.ignore-serial-consoles ds=nocloud;i=rpi-imager-1777416695538 cfg80211.ieee80211_regdom=US usb-storage.quirks=152d:0562:u\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 9. Backup Created
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Before modifying cmdline.txt, a backup was created:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt.bak_phase17rd3_20260501_110508\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This backup preserves the pre-patch boot command line in case rollback is needed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 10. Verification After Reboot
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 After applying the patch, Mini Jarvis was rebooted. The system booted successfully and the GUI answered a Fast-mode question correctly.\
The active kernel command line confirmed the patch was loaded:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 usb-storage.quirks=152d:0562:u\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The kernel confirmed that UAS was ignored for the JMicron bridge and usb-storage was used instead:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 usb 3-2: UAS is ignored for this device, using usb-storage instead\
usb-storage 3-2:1.0: USB Mass Storage device detected\
usb-storage 3-2:1.0: Quirks match for vid 152d pid 0562: 800000\
scsi host0: usb-storage 3-2:1.0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A direct log write test also passed after the patch:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 direct post quirk write test at Fri 1 May 11:18:29 CDT 2026\
WRITE TEST PASS\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 11. Final Phase Result
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\fi-180\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	JMicron SSD bridge identified: PASS\
\'95	UAS instability confirmed: PASS\
\'95	cmdline.txt backup created: PASS\
\'95	usb-storage quirk added: PASS\
\'95	Mini Jarvis rebooted correctly: PASS\
\'95	Mini Jarvis GUI launched: PASS\
\'95	Fast-mode answer worked: PASS\
\'95	Kernel confirmed UAS ignored for this device: PASS\
\'95	Direct conversation-log write test passed: PASS\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Final status: Phase 17R-D3 COMPLETE / PASSED.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 12. Current Operating Interpretation
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The original logging warning should now be understood as a storage-path symptom. Phase 17R made the logging layer non-fatal so the user still received an answer. Phase 17R-D3 addressed the likely root cause by disabling UAS for the unstable JMicron USB storage bridge.\
The log folder remains:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 /home/minijarvis/minijarvis/logs/conversations/\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Daily logs remain named:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 conversation_YYYY-MM-DD.txt\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Retention policy remains 60 days.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 13. Monitoring Recommendation
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 After Phase 17R-D3, Mini Jarvis should be allowed to run normally on Fast mode for an overnight stability watch. The following will be checked the next day:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\fi-180\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'95	Mini Jarvis remains responsive.\
\'95	Mouse and desktop menus remain normal.\
\'95	SSH by hostname still works.\
\'95	Conversation logging continues to work.\
\'95	No new UAS aborts or USB device resets appear in dmesg.\
\'95	No new Errno 5 input/output error appears in the GUI.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa180\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 14. Rollback Note
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Rollback should not be performed unless the usb-storage quirk causes a new problem. If rollback is required, restore the backed-up cmdline.txt or remove only the following parameter from /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt:\
\pard\pardeftab720\li360\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 usb-storage.quirks=152d:0562:u\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\partightenfactor0
\cf0 After rollback, reboot is required for the change to take effect.\
}